{"text": " I didn't tell my girlfriend that her pet had died. She found out about it only after returning from her trip. His name was Gus. He was a pet snake she'd had since she was eight. Yes, a snake. For some people, it's a strange pet, but for her, it was part of the family. Gus was old. We understood that he didn't have much time left. But when he died, I still couldn't stand it and cried. And my girlfriend was in another country at the time, on her brother's birthday. She had a complicated relationship with her family for a long time, and only recently they started getting along. She really wanted to get closer to her relatives again, and this trip was important to her. And now I had to decide what to do. Call and tell her that Gus died? She would be terribly upset, and the whole trip could go to hell. Or let her spend these few days with her family, and then tell everything in person. I chose the second option. When she arrived, I met her at the airport and told her the truth. I told her that Gus died, and that I didn't tell her anything on purpose while she was at the exit. She was silent the whole way home. At home, we put Gus in a pre-prepared box and buried him together. Then she told me, I still love you, but now I don't like you at all. I understood why she was angry and didn't argue. A little later, I prepared dinner. We sat down at the table and both cried. And before going to bed, I carefully asked if it was better for me to lie on the couch today. She answered that it would be the end for me if I slept somewhere other than our bed. No, we didn't break up. We are still together. And we both still lack gas. I don't regret that I waited for her return, but I perfectly understand why she was angry at me then.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 6.54, "text": " I didn't tell my girlfriend that her pet had died. She found out about it only after returning from her trip.", "tokens": [50364, 286, 994, 380, 980, 452, 10369, 300, 720, 381